WEBVTT

00:30.360 --> 00:31.150
Jean...

00:31.950 --> 00:33.950
Jean!

00:51.630 --> 00:52.300
Jean!

00:52.300 --> 00:53.800
Snap out of it!

00:53.800 --> 00:54.550
Please!

01:31.750 --> 01:33.670
It's no good, Professor X!

01:33.670 --> 01:36.550
Jean seems to have
completely lost control!

01:38.510 --> 01:40.310
She's being mind-controlled.

01:41.560 --> 01:44.890
She can't even respond to
my telepathy anymore.

01:47.810 --> 01:50.400
This must be the work
of Mastermind.

01:50.400 --> 01:51.980
It's too dangerous
to stay there.

01:53.030 --> 01:55.280
Jean's an omega-level psychic!

01:55.700 --> 01:58.240
If she goes cuts loose,
there ain't gonna be anywhere safe enough!

01:58.240 --> 01:59.280
Dammit!

01:59.950 --> 02:00.870
Jean!

02:01.740 --> 02:03.080
Cyclops. wait!

02:04.870 --> 02:05.660
Jean!

02:27.560 --> 02:28.230
J...

02:29.310 --> 02:30.270
Jean!

02:32.690 --> 02:33.940
Cyclops.

02:37.360 --> 02:38.150
Jean!?

02:38.780 --> 02:40.030
Please, Scott...

02:40.700 --> 02:42.120
you have to kill me.

02:42.660 --> 02:44.830
You know I can't do that!

02:44.830 --> 02:48.290
If this goes on, I'll kill you,
and our friends...

02:48.290 --> 02:50.250
and go on to destroy the world.

02:50.250 --> 02:55.510
Jean, you're just being manipulated
by the Inner Circle!

02:55.510 --> 02:57.170
If you can just
take control back...

02:57.170 --> 02:58.380
...I can't.

02:58.380 --> 02:59.470
It's okay!

02:59.470 --> 03:00.760
I'm here with you!

03:01.180 --> 03:01.800
Jean!

03:02.390 --> 03:03.350
I love you!

03:10.810 --> 03:12.270
It's you...

03:12.270 --> 03:14.150
you're the one controlling
Jean's mind!

03:15.570 --> 03:16.480
Jean!?

03:16.480 --> 03:17.570
What are you doing!?

03:22.120 --> 03:23.910
Jean's body!?

03:25.660 --> 03:27.160
Is she going to tear
herself apart!?

03:27.870 --> 03:28.500
J...

03:28.830 --> 03:30.120
Jean, don't!

03:34.540 --> 03:37.880
I love you, Scott.

03:41.800 --> 03:42.760
Jean!

05:20.070 --> 05:23.610
Accidents that occur in the growth of
organisms that precipitate evolution.

05:23.610 --> 05:24.990
Mutations...

05:25.490 --> 05:31.450
But among those, it is those of us who have
the "X-Gene" that are known as mutants.

05:32.250 --> 05:35.790
But those gifts made it
common for mutants to be

05:32.290 --> 05:36.670
<b><i>The Return - Joining Forces</i></b>

05:35.790 --> 05:39.000
discriminated against by
the rest of humanity.

05:39.500 --> 05:46.010
I have created this, the Xavier Institute,
to help those mutants.

05:46.760 --> 05:52.720
Here, mutant children are protected from
the prejudices of human society,

05:52.720 --> 05:57.770
and at the same time, taught how to use their powers
to protect a world that hates and fears them.

05:58.730 --> 06:01.190
So that some of them
may go on to join a team

06:01.190 --> 06:04.860
of exceptional mutants who fight for
the peaceful co-existence with humanity...

06:05.360 --> 06:07.150
The X-Men.

06:08.110 --> 06:15.200
But currently, neither the Xavier Institute
nor the X-Men are active.

06:16.250 --> 06:17.160
Yes...

06:17.160 --> 06:23.630
in the aftermath of a terrible battle a year ago
against a group of mutant criminals

06:23.630 --> 06:28.550
known as the Inner Circle.

06:29.470 --> 06:32.970
The X-Men have disbanded
since the day that Jean Grey,

06:32.970 --> 06:37.390
an extraordinary mutant and a beloved member
of this family, was lost...

07:09.760 --> 07:11.550
What's the matter, everyone?

07:13.510 --> 07:15.850
Now, come here...

07:18.390 --> 07:21.060
So, what exactly is bothering you?

07:22.190 --> 07:23.650
It's okay.

07:23.650 --> 07:28.950
As long as you are here,
your teachers and I will protect you.

07:37.790 --> 07:38.700
You're?

07:43.460 --> 07:44.380
Wait, please!

07:45.170 --> 07:47.590
I can't read your mind!

07:48.970 --> 07:49.920
Who...

07:50.840 --> 07:52.130
who are you?

08:01.100 --> 08:04.940
The same dream?

08:20.410 --> 08:21.830
Who...

08:21.830 --> 08:22.960
who is it!?

08:57.070 --> 09:01.830
I'm sure you must know,
but the institute is currently on hiatus.

09:04.620 --> 09:06.670
I understand.

09:06.670 --> 09:10.500
In that case, I'll do all I can to help.

09:11.460 --> 09:12.130
Goodbye.

09:55.590 --> 09:56.630
Pirates!

09:56.630 --> 09:57.970
It's a pirate boat!

09:59.850 --> 10:03.100
What's going to happen...

10:03.100 --> 10:05.680
Everyone, please stand back.

10:07.230 --> 10:08.440
You're?

10:28.420 --> 10:29.710
You'll be safe now.

10:30.880 --> 10:32.630
Hell yeah!

10:33.550 --> 10:35.420
Oh, thank you so much!

10:35.420 --> 10:37.720
Aren't you one of the X-Men?

10:38.220 --> 10:39.140
I am.

10:41.260 --> 10:42.350
Pardon me...

11:10.170 --> 11:12.750
This creature, you'll find,

11:12.750 --> 11:15.750
has had it's mental capacity elevated
to the level of homo sapiens...

11:15.750 --> 11:19.880
Mollusca cephalopod,
specimen designation #10...

11:20.720 --> 11:23.100
In other words, a squid.

11:28.430 --> 11:30.480
Using this wireless
underwater transmitter,

11:30.480 --> 11:33.980
we should be able to
communicate with him via speaker.

11:37.940 --> 11:39.610
What the hell is
he babbling about?

11:40.610 --> 11:42.780
Woo, we got ourselves
a real nutjob here!

11:53.790 --> 11:55.590
If you'll excuse me,
an urgent matter has come up.

11:55.590 --> 11:59.050
Mr. Devilfish here will continue
the lesson while I'm gone.

11:59.550 --> 12:02.180
He said a squid's gonna
give the lecture!

12:04.140 --> 12:05.600
Silence!

12:07.470 --> 12:10.230
Now, before we continue...

12:11.060 --> 12:13.060
Does anyone have any questions?

12:23.700 --> 12:25.200
Again!?

12:25.200 --> 12:28.870
Sir, you must be carrying more metal.

12:28.870 --> 12:31.040
I ain't "carrying" anything!

12:31.040 --> 12:32.500
I took it all off!

12:32.500 --> 12:35.210
Well, you're still setting
the metal detector off, so...

12:38.090 --> 12:40.800
Look, I can't exactly take these off...

12:43.010 --> 12:43.880
Here, see?

12:43.880 --> 12:45.220
Can I go now?

12:45.220 --> 12:46.600
But still...

12:52.060 --> 12:53.730
Cancel that trip to Madripoor...

12:55.060 --> 12:57.230
Gimme a ticket to New York.

13:15.870 --> 13:17.040
Charles!

13:21.090 --> 13:22.510
Welcome home, Ororo.

13:22.510 --> 13:23.470
It's good to be back...

13:27.800 --> 13:30.310
Can I get a little bit of a warning
next time you call me up?

13:30.310 --> 13:32.930
My vacation to
Madripoor's blown, now...

13:34.730 --> 13:36.730
How's it going, Charlie?

13:37.400 --> 13:38.900
Very well, Logan.

13:45.070 --> 13:47.870
It's wonderful to see you all again!

13:48.740 --> 13:53.450
The day-to-day academic routine was
beginning to get a bit tiresome...

13:53.450 --> 13:55.870
I'm truly glad to see all of you again.

13:57.420 --> 13:58.670
Where's Cyclops?

13:59.840 --> 14:02.500
He should have
received the call, but...

14:17.810 --> 14:19.310
One week ago,

14:19.310 --> 14:21.610
in the Tohoku region of Japan,

14:21.610 --> 14:26.450
a middle-schooler named Hisako lchiki
went missing on her way home from school.

14:26.990 --> 14:31.990
Since they were unable to find any leads,
Hisako's parents asked me for help...

14:31.990 --> 14:35.870
If they called the institute,
does that mean Hisako is?

14:36.370 --> 14:37.710
Yes, a mutant.

14:37.710 --> 14:41.500
Her powers manifested once,
when she was younger.

14:42.090 --> 14:43.380
Only once?

14:43.960 --> 14:46.760
Hisako's father is
an old friend of mine.

14:47.380 --> 14:49.930
The lchiki family is
a long line of mutants,

14:49.930 --> 14:52.600
but her parents never actually
manifested their powers.

14:53.180 --> 14:58.100
Prior to this incident, Hisako was living a
life no different than an average human...

14:58.850 --> 15:02.230
Don't that make this
a job for the cops?

15:02.230 --> 15:04.860
Unfortunately, once they begun
looking into her disappearance,

15:04.860 --> 15:08.240
several members of
the Japanese police have been killed,

15:08.240 --> 15:10.410
which has put a halt to
any progress on the investigation.

15:10.990 --> 15:15.120
Interference from people who would
rather Hisako never be found...

15:15.120 --> 15:16.250
Impossible!

15:16.250 --> 15:17.450
Mutants being hunted...

15:17.910 --> 15:20.750
There had been a rise in
the number of mutant manifestations

15:20.750 --> 15:22.500
in the Tohoku region over
the last few years,

15:22.500 --> 15:25.460
but now,
even with Cerebro's help,

15:25.460 --> 15:28.380
I have been unable to detect
any mutants there at all.

15:29.800 --> 15:35.260
Don't that just mean your
fancy mutant tracker's busted?

15:35.260 --> 15:37.850
Either that, or your powers
or starting to fritz out...

15:38.390 --> 15:39.560
Logan!

15:40.850 --> 15:42.520
I'm just joking.

15:42.520 --> 15:43.980
Take it easy.

15:44.980 --> 15:46.190
Professor...

15:47.280 --> 15:50.490
It actually may be
a malfunction with Cerebro.

15:50.490 --> 15:51.780
I'll check it out.

15:52.700 --> 15:55.950
Either way, there may be much more
to Hisako's disappearance

15:55.950 --> 15:58.500
than appearances
would suggest.

15:59.160 --> 16:03.000
The X-Men are to head to Japan,
and rescue Hisako.

16:03.420 --> 16:09.420
If there is something more to this,
then we'll need Cyclops.

16:20.730 --> 16:22.390
For Christs sake...

16:22.390 --> 16:24.690
you've been here
the whole time?

16:25.560 --> 16:27.150
Where'd you use the can?

16:34.490 --> 16:36.410
There was nothing wrong
with Cerebro.

16:37.200 --> 16:41.750
I was able to detect mutants all over
Japan, except within Tohoku.

16:41.750 --> 16:44.500
I didn't believe it was
a malfunction, but...

16:46.040 --> 16:51.090
That means that something in
Tohoku is blocking Cerebro.

16:51.090 --> 16:54.590
And it may be connected to
Hisako's disappearance.

16:55.010 --> 16:58.350
I'm sure we'll be able to get
the specifics once we're in Japan.

17:00.060 --> 17:05.310
Still, do you think it was a good idea to send
Wolverine to bring Cyclops back?

17:06.150 --> 17:09.360
That's why I had Storm
accompany him.

17:11.940 --> 17:13.950
I'm through with fighting.

17:13.950 --> 17:16.070
I lost too much because of it.

17:16.070 --> 17:17.910
That's not what we're here for, Scott.

17:17.910 --> 17:22.960
This isn't a fight, it's a mission to
rescue a missing mutant girl.

17:22.960 --> 17:25.790
I'd bet money we end up throwing down
with a buncha dirtbags

17:25.790 --> 17:27.790
on our way to find her, though.

17:27.790 --> 17:28.790
Wolverine!

17:29.550 --> 17:32.210
Storm, let's get outta here.

17:32.670 --> 17:36.640
This washout would just get in
our way if he came along.

17:37.800 --> 17:41.600
Sulking out here by himself
for a whole damned year...

17:43.270 --> 17:45.190
I bet if Jean saw you now,

17:45.190 --> 17:48.360
she'd finally realize
what a loser you are.

17:54.990 --> 17:55.900
Wolverine!

17:59.280 --> 18:00.200
Hey, bub!

18:00.200 --> 18:02.200
That wasn't funny.

18:02.200 --> 18:05.710
If it wasn't for my healing factor,
you coulda really done some damage!

18:07.750 --> 18:09.170
I was holding back that time.

18:10.040 --> 18:11.590
Push me again and
see what happens.

18:11.920 --> 18:13.210
You little...

18:16.170 --> 18:17.180
That's enough!

18:23.850 --> 18:27.020
Wolverine, why are you doing this?

18:27.020 --> 18:30.610
You're as worried about Scott
as the rest of us are.

18:35.490 --> 18:36.400
Scott...

18:36.990 --> 18:40.950
This missing child,
Hisako lchiki, needs help.

18:40.950 --> 18:43.660
But so do we...

18:45.950 --> 18:48.370
The X-Men need you.

18:52.420 --> 18:54.000
We'll be waiting for you.

18:54.710 --> 18:56.880
I'm sure Jean would want that.

19:00.090 --> 19:01.970
Let's go, Wolverine.

19:20.320 --> 19:21.660
<i>It's beautiful.</i>

19:22.160 --> 19:28.790
<i>The light of the sun, and the stars,
they shine for everyone equally.</i>

19:31.420 --> 19:33.670
<i>For humans, and mutants...</i>

19:36.800 --> 19:41.390
<i>Scott, the X-Men are like
a light in the darkness for mutants.</i>

19:41.390 --> 19:43.720
<i>I want to be part of that light.</i>

19:44.100 --> 19:48.770
<i>I want to brighten the future, for mutant
and human children all over the world...</i>

20:23.640 --> 20:24.640
What is it?

20:24.640 --> 20:27.310
Thought I smelt something familiar...

20:32.350 --> 20:36.650
Well, you're looking like your usual
one-eyed self again, Summers.

20:38.110 --> 20:39.780
We're on-duty Wolverine.

20:39.780 --> 20:41.400
Call me Cyclops.

20:44.740 --> 20:50.500
The X-Men have always been there
to help those in need.

20:51.580 --> 20:52.540
Scott...

20:53.040 --> 20:57.250
A young girl in Japan is
waiting for our help.

20:58.800 --> 21:01.880
Welcome home, Cyclops.

21:13.980 --> 21:15.770
You ain't flown anything in a whole year...

21:15.770 --> 21:18.060
you get your license renewed, bub?

21:18.060 --> 21:22.400
At the very least, I can still fly better
than you can drive a motorcycle.

23:03.710 --> 23:08.380
The X-Men have been reunited with their
leader, Cyclops, and they fly to Tohoku.

23:08.970 --> 23:10.470
As they looking for the missing girl,

23:10.470 --> 23:14.390
it becomes obvious that Hisako is not
the only mutant who has gone missing...

23:14.890 --> 23:21.020
And before long, a group of rogue scientists,
the U-Men, stand in their way.

23:21.650 --> 23:26.030
After infiltrating their base, the X-Men are
faced with a frightening realization...

23:26.570 --> 23:31.060
<b><i>U-MEN - Mutant Hunt</i></b>

23:26.650 --> 23:29.450
Next time on X-Men: Mutant Hunt
